   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "I added `Ledger.deposit(name, amount)` and `Ledger.withdraw(name, amount)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`, and the full suite passes (7 tests: 2 existing, 5 new).\n\n- **`deposit`:** it raises `ValueError` if the amount isn't positive. Otherwise it adds the amount to the account.\n- **`withdraw`:** it raises `ValueError` if the amount isn't positive, or if the withdrawal would take the account below zero. A failed withdrawal leaves the balance unchanged. Withdrawing the exact balance is allowed.\n- **Amount types:** both methods take a `str`, `int` or `Decimal`, and pass it through `Decimal(...)`. I avoided floats because they lose precision.\n- **Tests:** the new tests in `tests/test_ledger.py` cover these cases:\n  - deposit increases the balance;\n  - deposit rejects a zero or negative amount;\n  - withdraw decreases the balance, including down to exactly zero;\n  - withdraw refuses an overdraft;\n  - withdraw rejects a zero or negative amount.\n\nThe existing `transfer` can still take a source account below zero. You didn't ask me to change it, so I left it alone. If you want the same no-overdraft rule there, it's a small change.",
